Appendix F — Dimensional Analysis of the Virtualisation Decision Boundary

The main text proposes that the boundary between the virtualised and expansionist attractors is given by equality of marginal survival gains per joule:

\frac{\partial U}{\partial I}\,\eta = \frac{\partial U}{\partial A}\,\frac{1}{\gamma E^{\delta}} .

Here

· \partial U/\partial I has units of utility per bit.
· \eta has units of bits per joule (Landauer efficiency). Hence the left‑hand side has units utility per joule.
· \partial U/\partial A has units utility per square metre.
· \gamma E^{\delta} is the power required to maintain a unit of area (W m⁻²), i.e. J s⁻¹ m⁻², so 1/(\gamma E^{\delta}) has units m² J⁻¹. The right‑hand side therefore also has units utility per joule.

The equation is dimensionally consistent. In the earlier draft, a spurious division by E_{\text{bit}} was present; this has been removed.

